+*--indicator-panel* <path>
+	Draw the panel described by the state file _path_ underneath the
+	indicator. The file is a short list of _key value_ lines naming a PNG
+	beside it, the logical size to draw it at, a serial that changes when the
+	image changes, and a wall-clock stamp; the panel disappears again once
+	that stamp is older than its own _stale_ seconds. Setting _ring 0_ hides
+	swaylock's own arc, its borders and its per-keypress highlight for as long
+	as the panel is up, leaving the clock and the state message.
+
+	Nothing in the file is executed and no library is loaded from it: a
+	missing, unreadable, oversized, malformed, stale or foreign-owned file
+	means no panel is drawn, and the lock screen is exactly the one it would
+	have been without this option.
+
 *-R, --ready-fd* <fd>
 	Write a newline to the file descriptor _fd_ and close it once the
 	session is locked. Callers that wait on this notification never trust
